## 🟡 Medium — Missing Negative / Edge-Case Tests

No test covers error paths or boundary conditions. Production bugs often live here.

| Missing test | Why it matters |
|---|---|
| `UpdatePrice` with nonexistent SKU | Should throw `KeyNotFoundException` — untested |
| `GetProduct` with nonexistent SKU | Should return `null` — untested |
| `ImportFromCsv` with malformed input | Will throw `IndexOutOfRangeException` — no guard, untested |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount` with `fraction ≥ 1` | Would zero-out or go negative — untested |
| `ExportToCsv` on empty catalog | Edge case, empty string — untested |
| Multi-line CSV import | Only 1 line tested; `\n` splitting is untested |

```csharp
// Example fix for UpdatePrice negative path:
[TestMethod]
[ExpectedException(typeof(KeyNotFoundException))]
public void UpdatePrice_NonexistentSku_Throws()
{
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("MISSING", 5.00m);
}
```

