## Summary

| Severity | Count | Pattern |
|---|---|---|
| 🔴 Critical | 6 | Assert-free — calls method, discards result |
| 🟠 High | 4 | `IsNotNull`-only — verifies existence, not correctness |
| 🟡 Medium | 6+ | Missing negative/edge-case coverage |

**Root cause:** Every test follows the same template — call the method, maybe check `IsNotNull`, move on. This gives the coverage tool a line-hit on every production branch while verifying almost nothing. The fix is to **assert on the actual values and side-effects** of each operation, and add negative-path tests for error handling.
